# Summary
A security-relevant bug is introduced: response header values derived from query parameters are not validated for control characters before being emitted as headers.
The commit adds apply_response_overrides for GetObject responses. It takes attacker-controlled query parameters (response-content-type, response-content-disposition, etc.) and inserts them directly into response headers. These values are percent-decoded without any validation or filtering of control characters, unlike stored metadata which is validated elsewhere. If the HTTP header builder accepts CR/LF or other control bytes, an attacker could craft a URL with %0d%0a to inject arbitrary headers or split responses, enabling cache poisoning or client-side attacks. This path is new to the commit and does not enforce the existing invalid-header-byte checks.

